@startuml
' Current runtime model and latest provider snapshots.
hide methods
entity "Smurfs" as SmurfTable {
  * Id : Guid <<PK>>
  --
  * Name : string
  * CreatedUtc : DateTime
  * Health : int
  Birthday : DateTime?
  Infected : bool?
  Gender : int?
  PetId : Guid? <<FK, indexed>>
  VillageId : Guid? <<shadow FK, indexed>>
}
entity "Pets" as PetTable {
  * Id : Guid <<PK>>
  --
  * Name : string
}
entity "Villages" as VillageTable {
  * Id : Guid <<PK>>
  --
  * Name : string
}
SmurfTable "0..*" --> "0..1" PetTable : PetId
SmurfTable "0..*" --> "0..1" VillageTable : VillageId
note bottom of VillageTable
  Accepted (ADR 0001): optional one-to-many membership.
  Smurfs.VillageId references Villages.Id; NULL = no village.
  VillageId is an EF shadow property, absent from C# Smurf.
  Pet FK: explicit Restrict.
  Village FK: explicit ClientSetNull.
end note
note bottom of PetTable
  PostgreSQL baseline 20261118194640_InitialPostgres
  and the SQLite baseline share these tables and relationships.
  PostgreSQL uses uuid for Guid, text for string, and integer for Health.
  SQLite uses TEXT for Guid/string and INTEGER for Health.
  Pet FK: ON DELETE RESTRICT; Village FK: no cascade.
  Later migrations rename Age to Health and add optional attributes.
  Current snapshots include all fields shown.
end note
note bottom of SmurfTable
  Birthday, Infected, and Gender are optional in the runtime model.
  Gender is stored as an integer by EF convention (Male=0, Female=1).
  Both providers include migrations for these properties.
end note
note bottom of SmurfTable
  CreatedUtc is required in the runtime model.
  CreatedUtc provider migrations are included.
  Existing rows use the generated year-0001 default.
end note
@enduml
